.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH choom-host 1  "choom-host " 
.SH NAME
choom\-host \- Share your local shell through a relay
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBchoom\-host\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-shell\fR] [\fB\-\-record\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-identity\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-default\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-fingerprint\fR] [\fB\-\-detach\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Share your local shell through a relay
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
YAML config file (CLI flags override its values)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Relay hostname [default: choom.sh]
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCHOOM_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Relay SSH port [default: 2200]
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCHOOM_PORT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Shell to run (defaults to $SHELL, then /bin/sh)
.TP
\fB\-\-record\fR
Ask the relay to record this session
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Identity key file to authenticate with (overrides the default key)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-default\-key\fR
Do not use the bundled default key (use \-i or a persisted per\-user key)
.TP
\fB\-\-fingerprint\fR \fI<FINGERPRINT>\fR
Verify the relay\*(Aqs host\-key fingerprint (`SHA256:…`) on connect
.TP
\fB\-\-detach\fR
Detached "remote\-support" mode: share the shell to viewers without attaching your local terminal (print the links, then relay; the shell is driven remotely)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  Share your shell on the default relay:
      choom host
  Point at your own relay and record the session:
      choom host \-s relay.example.com \-\-record
  Use a specific identity on a private relay:
      choom host \-s relay.example.com \-\-no\-default\-key \-i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
